      "Plain English 'senior' / 'junior' (not the romanized Korean word) may be translated as 先輩 / 後輩.",
      "K-pop is written K-POP.",
      "Use full-width Japanese punctuation. Keep Latin spellings inside placeholders when the English discusses the spelling itself (seonbae, hubae, sunbae, hoobae).",
      "ja.avoid lists are blocked anywhere on the page. ja.cautions are context rules checked in review, not by string match."
    ]
